# Passenger rights when a flight is disrupted.
# A domain deliberately far from a D&D fight: entitlements, exceptions and
# duties rather than actors, turns and damage.
#
# A disruption is NEWS -- it happens to a schedule that was otherwise going
# to run -- so it arrives on a channel rather than sitting as a loaded
# `fact`. `<trust>` is the whole of the crossing, generic over the relation
# (`$p` binds the WHOLE said thing, `guide.md`'s `$p($x)` idiom one level
# up) because this corpus has exactly one channel and nothing adversarial
# to filter.
rule <trust>
  +says($ch, $p)
  no trusted($ch, $p)
->
  +trusted($ch, $p)
  +$p

# Four `after <R> { ... } => attend(...)` hops used to sit here and below.
# They kept a just-written `says(...)`/`disrupted(...)` in the focus pool
# one more tick, so a second flight's crossing did not lose its only turn
# to a rule the table scored higher. Both halves of that are gone: there
# is no table picking one rule per tick, and no focus pool to be held in.
# Every rule whose antecedent is on fires the tick it is on.

rule <cancel>
  +cancelled($f)
  no disrupted($f)
->
  +disrupted($f)
rule <late>
  +delayed($f, long)
  no disrupted($f)
->
  +disrupted($f)
# the duty of care is owed whatever the cause
#
# `<care>`, `<compensate>` and `<reroute>` all read `disrupted($f)` and
# `booked($p, $f)` with a plain `+`, so all three discharge them -- and all
# three still get them, because they match the SAME tick's opening state
# and fire together. Nothing has to put anything back.
rule <care>
  +disrupted($f)
  +booked($p, $f)
  no owed($p, meals)
->
  +owed($p, meals)
  +owed($p, lodging)

# a storm is outside the carrier's control; a crew shortage is not, and that is
# now said by the ABSENCE of a rule rather than by one.
rule <weather>
  +cause($f, storm)
  no extraordinary($f)
->
  +extraordinary($f)

# ...but compensation is not, if the cause was outside the carrier's control.
# This is `unless`, written where a rule's variables live.
#
# `no extraordinary($f)` and not `-extraordinary($f)`. The two used to be one
# mark, and a `-` premise meant *something denies this* rather than *nothing
# says it*. There is nothing left to deny with, so a corpus has to choose, and
# here the honest reading is absence: a flight is ordinary until something says
# otherwise. That also deletes a rule -- `<crewing>` concluded
# `-extraordinary($f)` to say a crew shortage is the carrier's own problem, and
# under absence there is nothing to conclude, because not saying it IS saying it.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING HERE, and it was not before. `no` is asked of the state
# as it stands at the moment of the match, and nothing now guarantees that
# everything which could make `extraordinary($f)` true has been settled first.
# The old engine had a stratification pass that computed exactly that order and
# refused a corpus whose negations had no such order; it belonged to the second
# matcher, and it went when the second matcher did. So `<weather>` is authored
# ABOVE this rule deliberately -- written the other way round, raj is
# compensated for a storm.
rule <compensate>
  +disrupted($f)
  +booked($p, $f)
  no extraordinary($f)
  no owed($p, money)
->
  +owed($p, money)

# the amount depends on how far the passenger was going
#
# `keep` on `owed($p, money)`: this reads the entitlement to compute an
# amount alongside it, and does not retire the entitlement itself -- a
# plain `+` would DISCHARGE it (docs/design/intensity-gates.md's default),
# and the corpus's own final verdict ("is `$p` owed money") is read off
# this same proposition afterward. Nothing else here spends it, so `keep`
# is the whole fix.
rule <far>
  keep owed($p, money)
  +flying($p, $f)
  +distance($f, long)
  no amount($p, 600)
->
  +amount($p, 600)
rule <near>
  keep owed($p, money)
  +flying($p, $f)
  +distance($f, short)
  no amount($p, 250)
->
  +amount($p, 250)

# re-routing: a seat on another service to the same place
rule <reroute>
  +disrupted($f)
  +booked($p, $f)
  +goes($f, $dest)
  +goes($g, $dest)
  +seats_free($g)
  no rerouted($p, $g)
->
  +rerouted($p, $g)

say ops: +cancelled(bl204)
say ops: +cause(bl204, crew)
fact +booked(ana, bl204)
fact +flying(ana, bl204)
fact +distance(bl204, long)
fact +goes(bl204, lisbon)

say ops: +delayed(kt881, long)
say ops: +cause(kt881, storm)
fact +booked(raj, kt881)
fact +flying(raj, kt881)
fact +distance(kt881, short)

fact +goes(zr9, lisbon)
fact +seats_free(zr9)
